---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How this site handles enquiry data, technical records and future analytics choices."
  path="/privacy/"
  updated="24 Aug 2026"
>
  <h2>Scope of this draft</h2>
  <p>
    This notice covers the public DataDecision website and its diagnostic enquiry form. It does not
    yet describe client-project data processing, which requires engagement-specific terms and, where
    appropriate, a data-processing agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you choose to provide</h2>
  <p>
    The enquiry form asks for your name, work email, company or website, role, primary problem,
    preferred timeline, optional project-budget band and consent to a response. Hidden fields may
    capture campaign parameters and the referring page so the enquiry source can be understood.
  </p>
  <p>
    The form also uses a honeypot field and a minimum-completion-time check to reduce automated
    spam. The client-side check is not described as server-side rate limiting.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens before the form endpoint is configured</h2>
  <p>
    If the production form provider has not been configured, the website does not transmit the form
    and does not report a successful submission. The missing connection is shown to the visitor.
  </p>

  <h2>Purposes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Review and respond to a requested diagnostic or partnership enquiry.</li><li>
      Assess fit and prepare a written scope.
    </li><li>Protect the form and diagnose delivery failures.</li><li>
      Understand aggregate enquiry sources after an approved analytics setup exists.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Retention and recipients</h2>
  <p>
    The final retention period, form provider, recipient workflow and deletion process require
    founder approval before launch. DataDecision should retain enquiry data only as long as needed
    for the stated purpose, legal obligations and legitimate record-keeping, and should document
    every provider that receives it.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    No third-party analytics or non-essential cookie is installed in this build. The site emits
    first-party browser events that remain in the page unless an approved analytics adapter is
    added. See the <a href="/cookies/">cookie policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    To ask about information supplied through this site, email <a
      href="mailto:u22me137@med.svnit.ac.in">u22me137@med.svnit.ac.in</a
    >. A reviewed version must still identify the legal entity and jurisdiction-specific rights
    request process; this draft does not claim a universal legal basis.
  </p>

  <h2>Security and limits</h2>
  <p>
    Static delivery reduces some server-side attack surface, but no website can promise absolute
    security. Provider access, retention, authentication and incident response must be verified
    before production.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
